# G8 (text): the mouse in the file dialog's Open and Insert Picture. A folder of 16 entries, more than the list shows: the scroll bar's
# arrows move one entry and its track a page, a click on the empty part of the list does nothing, the Name header sorts, a double click on
# a file opens it, the Open button opens the selected file, Cancel ends the dialog, and Insert > Picture takes a picture by a double click.
@dialog
@dir QUILL
@place Quill C:\QUILL
@cwd C:\DOCS
@many DOCS 14 QLD
@copy letter.qld DOCS\
@copy pic.bmp DOCS\
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.QLD 2026-11-24 18:45
@stamp DOCS\PIC.BMP 2026-11-20 10:00
@click 3 0                    # File menu
@click 4 3                    # Open...: the dialog
@click 52 15                  # the scroll bar's down arrow: one entry
@click 52 15
@click 52 4                   # its up arrow: one entry back
@click 52 13                  # the track below the thumb: the end of the list
@click 52 5                   # the track above the thumb: the top again
@click 30 3                   # the Name header: sorted by name, descending
@click 30 3                   # and ascending again
@click 20 10                  # an entry: selected
@click 25 18                  # the empty row under the list: nothing
@click 53 4                   # beside the list: nothing
@click 67 19                  # Cancel: the dialog ends
@click 3 0
@click 4 3
@click 52 13                  # the end of the list
@click 20 15                  # LETTER.QLD
@click 55 19                  # Open: that file is opened
@click 3 0
@click 4 3
@click 52 13
@dclick 20 15                 # a double click opens a file
@click 14 0                   # Insert menu
@click 16 2                   # Picture...: the Insert Picture dialog
@click 20 5                   # PIC.BMP: selected
@click 67 19                  # Cancel
